    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7989A\n\nSPONSOR: LITTLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the executive law, in relation to\ndesignating Minerva Lake and Minerva Stream as inland waterways for\npurposes of waterfront revitalization\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill designates Minerva Lake and Minerva Stream as inland waterways\nfor purposes of waterfront revitalization.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends paragraphs (a) and (c) of subdivision 4 of section 911\nof the executive law, as separately amended by chapters 43, 255 and 433\nof the laws of 2017 and subdivision (c) as separately amended by chap-\nters 43, 110, 142, 161 and 255 of the laws of 2017 to expand the defi-\nnition of \"inland waterways\" to include Minerva Lake and Minerva Stream.\n\nSection 2 establishes an effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMinerva Steam is the main tributary to the 88 acre Minerva Lake located\nin the town of Minerva, Essex County NY, with such lake and waterway\nbeing a key component of the Town of Minerva's economic well-being as\nits main tourist attraction.\n\nThe inclusion of the Minerva Stream and Minerva Lake within the inter-\ncostal waterway system will open eligibility for the Town of Minerva\nunder the Local Waterfront Revitalization Program as administered by the\nNew York State Department of State.\n\nAs part of the Local Waterfront Revitalization Program, the Town of\nMinerva can access the Division of Coastal Resources assistance in many\nways, which include but are not limited to the following; organizing the\nplanning process, establishing a waterfront advisory committee, assist-\nance with data collection and analysis, accessing information from other\ncommunities that have successfully revitalized their waterfronts,\nproviding guidance on developing appropriate waterfront revitalization\npolicies, assistance in identifying and with preparation of laws neces-\nsary to implement the Local Waterfront Revitalization Program and\nproviding grants for revitalization projects.\n\nThe inclusion of Minerva Lake and Minerva Stream would be beneficial to\nnot only the Town of Minerva, but for the County as a whole.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
